
The src/rp directory is a program-level directory contains a set of 
class templates that are defined in namespace Pscf::Rp, and that are used 
to construct the pscf_rpc and pscf_rpg programs for SCFT and PS-FTS 
calculations that involve real periodic fields. 

This directory and the associated namespace define of a set of class 
templates that are designed so that different specializations of each
template can be to construct programs that use different hardware.
Almost every class in this namespace takes two template parameters,
denoted by D and T. Parameter D is an integer parameter that represents
the dimension of space, which has allowed values D=1, 2, and 3. Parameter 
T is typename parameter that can be used to represent two "backend type" 
classes, named CPT and CUT, that are used to control what type of 
"backend" a specialization of the class will use for parallelizable 
operations. Template specializations with T=CUT use a GPU backend that 
is coded in CUDA, and are used to construct the pscf_rpg GPU-enabled 
program. Template specializations with T=CPT instead use only standard 
CPU hardware, and are used to construct the pscf_rpc CPU program. 

The CPT and CUT classes are defined in namespace Pscf, in files that are 
located in the pscf/backends directory.  

Subdirectories:

The src/rp directory has the subjectories listed below, giving a 
structure analogous to that of both the src/rpc and src/rpg directories:
  
field/        - fields and spatial domain
solvers/      - modified diffusion equation (MDE) solvers
system/       - main System class template
environment/  - mask and external fields for inhomogeneous environments
scft/         - self-consistent field theory (SCFT)
fts/          - partial saddle-point field theoretic simulation (PS-FTS)

Main programs:

The files pscf_rpc.cpp and pscf_rpg.cpp contain main functions for the
pscf_rpc and pscf_rpg programs. Both of these functions use a function
template that is defined in the file run.h.
